xlink:href="kjr-8-57-g001"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Fig. 2</label><caption><p>Stent fracture of the type 2 stent in a 64-year-old patient.180 days after stent insertion, the stent broke between theproximal end and the body (arrows).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-8-57-g002"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Fig. 3</label><caption><p>Inadequate expansion of the type 2 stent in a 60-year-old patient. Seven days after insertion, inadequate expansion of the stent was noted.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-8-57-g003"/></fig><fig id="F4" position="float"><label>Fig. 4</label><caption><p>Tumor ingrowth of the type 3 stent in a 65-year-old patient. 135 days after stent insertion, tumor ingrowth on the CT scan was seen (arrows). No symptomatic bowel obstruction was noted until the patient's death.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-8-57-g004"/></fig></floats-group></article>